34:["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Half-day (about 3–4 hours):"}]," the main sites with short stops."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Longer:"}]," if you want to climb Jabal al-Nour (the climb and descent alone take a couple of hours) or spend more time at Arafat."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Add Taif:"}]," for a full day, some families combine Makkah Ziyarat with a ",["$","$L25","a-0",{"href":"/services/taif-ziyarat","children":"Taif Ziyarat"}]," — ",["$","$L25","a-1",{"href":"/routes/makkah-to-taif","children":"Makkah to Taif"}]," is about 90 km, around 1 hour 10 minutes."]}],"\n"]}]
